:"genre","name":"Rock & Roll","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[{"id":198167102636761,"name":"Cantautoras de los noventa","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1989,"end":2003,"desc":"Las mujeres tienen sus propios estilos, en plural: Azalia Snail y su psicodelia lo-fi, Jarboe, Lida Husik (entre la cantante pop y la pintora sonora), Robin Holcomb, Lisa Germano (Geek The Girl, «un viaje dantesco a la psique de una chica»), Tori Amos, Juliana Hatfield, Kristin Hersh, Jewel, Natalie Merchant, Cat Power (Moon Pix), Edith Frost, Lauryn Hill, Shannon Wright. Las «grrrls» más airadas: Lois Maffeo, Ani DiFranco, PJ Harvey (Dry, Rid Of Me), Liz Phair (Exile In Guyville), DQE, Aimee Mann, Sheryl Crow, Alanis Morissette, Neko Case. Y los paisajes sonoros de Björk, la cantautora más influyente de la década, Kate St John, Natacha Atlas, Heather Duby, Solex y Beth Orton.","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#women-90s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":94719644319818,"artist":"Sheryl Crow","artist_id":267846320286284,"title":"Tuesday Night Music Club","year":1994,"ess":0,"yt":"ZSiyfOvlIRM","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautoras de los noventa","scene_id":198167102636761,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#women-90s","chapters":["Sección 6.6"],"pages":[[1,254,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":254,"text":"…on I'm With Stupid (1995). Two veterans climbed the charts in Los Angeles with a mainstream sound and a mood that were the outcome of these changes: Sheryl Crow, with Tuesday Night Music Club (1994), and Meredith Brooks, with Blurring The Edges (1997). A turning point was represented by the success of a…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Another Roadside Attraction International Tourmate","body":"Sheryl Crow was an international act that toured with The Tragically Hip's Another Roadside Attraction festival in 1993, 1995, and 1997, alongside Canadian performers. \"But they also brought along Midnight Oil, Blues Traveler, Matthew Sweet and Cheryl Crow.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 8: The CanRock Revolution","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U2kYleeMnl8"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Guest Musician on 12 Bar Blues","body":"Sheryl Crow was among the guest musicians brought in for Scott Weiland's solo album, 12 Bar Blues, where she played the accordion. This unusual choice of instrument for a rock record was noted as fascinating. \"All kinds of guest musicians were brought in, including people like Cheryl Crow. She was brought in to play of all things the accordion.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Going Solo","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-f9jhqAHkQo"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best Female Pop Vocal Performance (1995) — All I Wanna Do","body":"Won.","year":1995,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q935283"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best New Artist (1995)","body":"Nominated.","year":1995,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1453643"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Record of the Year (1995) — All I Wanna Do","body":"Won.","year":1995,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q843219"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"BRIT Award for International Female Solo Artist (1997)","body":"Won.","year":1997,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q16985325"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best Female Rock 